Package: winn
Title: White Noise Normalization for Metabolomics LC-MS Data
Version: 0.1.4
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "Tanmay", family = "Tanna", email = "tanmay@tanmaytanna.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
    )
Description: Provides a decision-guided workflow for correcting technical
    variability in metabolomics data, including liquid chromatography-mass
    spectrometry (LC-MS) data, while preserving metabolites that already
    satisfy a white-noise gatekeeper. The workflow combines robust outlier
    adjustment, adaptive drift detection, change-point
    segmentation, batch correction, and probabilistic quotient normalization
    in a single pipeline or as modular steps. It supports
    quality-control (QC)-informed parameter tuning as well as QC-agnostic
    operation for studies without pooled controls. The underlying white-noise
    normalization strategy is described by Demler et al. (2024)
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2404.07906>.
Depends: R (>= 3.5.0)
